(5879338, 853955, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that this a freaky subject but could be more dramatic<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> I think there is quite a conflict between the white snow and the dark masks. Because of this I find the snow grabs my attention more than the masks. Composition is good. A square crop may have allowed you to use more screen space and thus let us see a bit more of the detail in the masks.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> this has great potential. For more drama I might have looked at a B&amp;W conversion. <br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> a good shot that shows something unique but doesn''t quite fulfill it''s potential when it comes to making a dramatic statement. <br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that this a freaky subject but could be more dramatic Technically I think there is quite a conflict between the white snow and the dark masks. Because of this I find the snow grabs my attention more than the masks. Composition is good. A square crop may have allowed you to use more screen space and thus let us see a bit more of the detail in the masks. Artistically this has great potential. For more drama I might have looked at a B&W conversion.  In summary a good shot that shows something unique but doesn''t quite fulfill it''s potential when it comes to making a dramatic statement.  Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-24 13:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5879347, 853930, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are of a very dreamlike scene.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> this is a good shot as the result shows. I think the crop doesn''t show off the model to her potential - square might have been the way to got here. There seems to be a lot of noise(?) in the background that is quite distracting.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> you can''t go too wrong with a model like this. Her eyes look very unnatural however, more then the entire "unnatural" look that the lighting/processing gives.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> a great shot that has heaps of potential but a couple of nitpicks held it back from the top 10.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are of a very dreamlike scene. Technically this is a good shot as the result shows. I think the crop doesn''t show off the model to her potential - square might have been the way to got here. There seems to be a lot of noise(?) in the background that is quite distracting. Artistically you can''t go too wrong with a model like this. Her eyes look very unnatural however, more then the entire "unnatural" look that the lighting/processing gives. In summary a great shot that has heaps of potential but a couple of nitpicks held it back from the top 10. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-24 13:24:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5879397, 854162, 113278, '<td valign="top">Greeting from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>First Impressions: Excellent emotion catching shot, great photojournalism. <br/> <br/>Composition: The center framing on this works well and with this shot I feel as though the emotion captured outweighs any composition flaws. The focus is also spot on and nice details throughout. <br/> <br/>Lighting: Was this posed? I am thinking that it wasnt but either way I thin the lighting is excellent. No harsh shadows and no blown out areas. Well lit all throughout the shot.<br/> <br/>Artistic: This has it all, the look in his eyes, the dirt on his face and helmet all really tell a story. <br/> <br/>Challenge: This definitely meets the challenge and is unique and stands out. <br/> <br/>Overall I think this was a well done photo but it lacked a wow factor that many look for. Looking at your scores you received very few 4 or below which is excellent and you had a small audience that really appreciated this shot. As mentioned in the comments it would have been nice to eliminate the small portion of the mic but it also may have benefited from more of the mic but just that little piece seems out of place. <br/> <br/>Great job on this and well done on a new personal best.<br/></td>', 'Greeting from the Critique Club First Impressions: Excellent emotion catching shot, great photojournalism.  Composition: The center framing on this works well and with this shot I feel as though the emotion captured outweighs any composition flaws. The focus is also spot on and nice details throughout.  Lighting: Was this posed? I am thinking that it wasnt but either way I thin the lighting is excellent. No harsh shadows and no blown out areas. Well lit all throughout the shot. Artistic: This has it all, the look in his eyes, the dirt on his face and helmet all really tell a story.  Challenge: This definitely meets the challenge and is unique and stands out.  Overall I think this was a well done photo but it lacked a wow factor that many look for. Looking at your scores you received very few 4 or below which is excellent and you had a small audience that really appreciated this shot. As mentioned in the comments it would have been nice to eliminate the small portion of the mic but it also may have benefited from more of the mic but just that little piece seems out of place.  Great job on this and well done on a new personal best.', '2010-02-24 13:56:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5879533, 854021, 113278, '<td valign="top">Nice shot and the B&amp;W works excellent. The shadows also cars an almost eery feel to it and your angle is excellent. One of my favorites of the challenge.</td>', 'Nice shot and the B&W works excellent. The shadows also cars an almost eery feel to it and your angle is excellent. One of my favorites of the challenge.', '2010-02-24 14:45:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5879538, 853890, 113278, '<td valign="top">It looks like you put in a bit of thought for this one and it is well composed. Everything seems to be well done on this but it seems to lack something, a lasting memory I guess. It is good but I quess easily forgotten. At least you didn''t use the typical Cowboy hat like I did though lol, you definitely get points for originality.</td>', 'It looks like you put in a bit of thought for this one and it is well composed. Everything seems to be well done on this but it seems to lack something, a lasting memory I guess. It is good but I quess easily forgotten. At least you didn''t use the typical Cowboy hat like I did though lol, you definitely get points for originality.', '2010-02-24 14:49:32.000000', NULL, 0),
